Spring Boot Starter Dependencies
Introduction
One of the key features that makes Spring Boot developer-friendly is Starter Dependencies.
Starter Dependencies are pre-configured dependency bundles provided by Spring Boot that simplify project setup and dependency management.
Instead of adding multiple libraries individually, developers can add a single starter dependency and Spring Boot automatically includes all the required libraries.
This reduces complexity, avoids version conflicts, and accelerates development.
________________________________________
What Are Starter Dependencies?
Starter Dependencies are dependency descriptors that aggregate commonly used libraries for a specific purpose.
For example, when building a REST API, instead of manually adding:
•	Spring MVC
•	Embedded Tomcat
•	Jackson
•	Validation Libraries
you can simply add:
<dependency>
    <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
    <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-web</artifactId>
</dependency>
Spring Boot automatically includes all the required libraries.
________________________________________
