Summary
Starter Dependencies are one of the most useful features of Spring Boot. They simplify dependency management by grouping commonly used libraries into a single dependency.
This reduces configuration effort, prevents version conflicts, and allows developers to build applications faster and more efficiently.
Understanding Starter Dependencies is important because they work closely with Auto Configuration to make Spring Boot development fast and productive.
